\image(figures/individuals_moving_range.svg)
// result_end
\caption(Individual fill weights and adjacent moving ranges, with limits estimated from batches one through ten.)
\alttext(The individuals chart shows a sustained level shift. The moving-range chart emphasizes the jump into that level.)

> Interpret the chart

The individuals chart uses the baseline mean and estimates process standard
deviation from the mean baseline moving range divided by the normal range
factor for pairs. A moving range is indexed by the second observation in its
pair, so its first point is batch two. A lasting level shift can leave the
individuals chart outside its limits even after the adjacent ranges return to
their baseline scale.

> References

- [NIST individuals control charts|https://www.itl.nist.gov/div898/handbook/pmc/section3/pmc322.htm]
